// wolf_entropy.lu — dw02: what a wolf program's `os_random` gets on PAX.
// wolf's runtime makes the one call the spec names ([os.random.platform]:
// getrandom(2), flags 0, EINTR retried, a short read continued) and traps
// on any other failure ([os.random.trap]: no error row, no fallback). Built
// by tools/mkentropy with the pinned wolf, linked static (tools/mkwolf-hello's
// shape); run by tests/mpx6-entropy after the C probe. It prints the count it
// got, never a byte: a refused draw ends the program by its trap before the
// second line.
fn main() {
    print("wolf-entropy: os_random 32 asked\n")
    let b = os_random(32)
    let n = b.len
    print("wolf-entropy: os_random 32 gave {n}\n")
}
